WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:08.770
Can satellite images look sharper? This Stockholm example compares a 10-metre Sentinel-2 image with finer output grids.

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:17.570
Bicubic interpolation and SEN2SR produce 2.5-metre output pixels from the same input.

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:26.850
LDSR-S2 adds a different visual reconstruction. Sharper appearance is not proof of recovered detail.

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:36.450
The difference map measures spectral change, not factual correctness. Validate details against independent imagery.
